TEXT 432 -376 Left 2 ;---- 555 Timer ----
TEXT -1080 -256 Left 2 ;- Min input Voltage for OP27 = 11V\n- When Trigger pin goes low (less than 1/3 of Vcc) output goes high\n- Output V from chip ~ 1.5V lower than VCC when high & ~ 0V when low \n   - 555 timer can give out only 100 - 200 mA total\n- Reset pin resets entire circuit, its an "inverted pin".\nresets when pin goes low, normal state is high\n- Control Voltage pin controls threshold voltage of threshold pin.\nuseful to adjust frequency of circuit without changing R & C values.\ncan see this pin connected to small cap (0.01 uF/ 10nF) to ground -\nthis prevents noise from influencing frequency. can also be disconnected\n- Threshold pin sets output back to low when voltage goes high (above 2/3 of Vcc)\n- Pin 7 discharge, this pin is unconnected when output is high, connected\nto ground when output is low, connects to external timing components\n- Vcc = positive power supply pin, 5V < Vcc < 15V
